Learnings, this took some time to really understand and grasp the concept but after spending hours was finally able to understand : 

1. Double-entry exists because recording both ends of a movement makes errors detectable
2. Debit = destination (left), credit = source (right). Not “in” and “out”
3. Assets/expenses are where value lands; liabilities/equity/revenue are where value originates. That’s why Assets = Liabilities + Equity is a tautology, not a formula to memorize
4. Natural side = where a balance normally rests, not the only direction an account receives
5. Bank statements feel inverted because they’re the bank’s ledger, where your account is their liability
6. Revenue/liability accounts aren’t pots of money — they explain why you hold value. Cash lands in an asset; revenue records the reason
7. Bug found: the balance query assumes every account is an asset, so all liability/equity/revenue balances come back sign-flipped. allow_negative on opening_balances was masking it
